verdict.description:
    First-match-wins verdict:
    * servable — enough lines clear the floor for the patch-scoped surfaces to mean something;
* notAggregated — matches were ingested but no aggregate row exists yet. Wait, or check the fold;
* thin — aggregated, and still short of the bar. The patch genuinely lacks games;
* unknown — nothing ingested and nothing aggregated, so there is no reading to give.
    `notAggregated` and `thin` are kept apart on purpose: they are the two
    causes of the same low number and they call for opposite reactions.

lastHeartbeatAtUtc.description:
Last liveness heartbeat of an in-flight run, or null for legacy rows / runs
that never beat. The frontend can surface how fresh a `Running` row is;
the API has already aged a stale one out to "Abandoned" in ProcessRunStatus ProcessRunReadModel.Status.

patch.description:
The `major.minor` patch the window covers, on the patch series only;
`null` elsewhere, and also on the patch series when no
tracked match has a parseable patch yet (a fresh database).
